  "preconditions": [
    "Explicit csv-profile-v1 key and expected canonical hash; actual supplied profile and exchange-mapping-v1 bytes with source_format csv. No data-derived lookup or defaults."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Select exact resources, decode literal UTF-8 RFC-4180 datasets and roundtrip explicit records without changing identity, types, values, order or field presence.",
    "Reject ambiguous/unsupported declarations, wrong resource bindings and nonrepresentable values before returning a result; preserve passive inputs and no-write boundaries.",
    "Exercise the same bound dataset conversion in isolated Core and PYZ without optional packages.",
    "Exercise R edge cases: BOM as input signature versus literal U+FEFF, exact/reordered/missing headers, every explicit empty policy, invalid syntax/typed values, logical error coordinates, one canonical inverse value-map match, owned observations and unchanged real project inputs.",
    "Run the unchanged W/R and affected View export behavior contracts with the common pure CSV record serializer; verify original View scalar/typed control bytes separately from csv-profile-v1 rejection, without new coercion, output authority or source mutation."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Der CSV-Import und -Export MUSS RFC-4180-konforme Felder, Anführungszeichen, eingebettete Zeilenumbrüche, CRLF-Dateizeilen und UTF-8 unterstützen sowie ein optionales BOM ausschließlich beim Import akzeptieren.",
    "scope": "14.f.W/R/C pure bound dataset codec. W contracts and tests remain unchanged. R covers exact BOM/header/width and null/absence boundaries; strict types, finite JSON numbers, safe SRV090/3 bindings and logical record/column coordinates without raw cell leakage; complete-or-rejected observations and exports; foreign hooks, cycles, strict-reader nesting, large fields, unchanged global limits, owned resources/records, real read-only projects and isolated Core/PYZ. The additive external_fields operation inverses only the exact mapped native field projection, requiring one canonical target match and a representable external cell; it does not construct a whole-model export, identity, plan or publication authority. Canonical JSON export retains the W rejection of forbidden raw DEL. No complete CLI import/export, arbitrary model roundtrip, full runtime-budget integration, full-suite or release pass is claimed. C shares only byte framing/quoting/UTF-8 serialization. The View envelope, typed cells, generated metadata, exact bytes and existing errors remain unchanged. Dataset character and first-header U+FEFF admission stays with the bound profile adapter."
  },
